---
import './freshness.css';
---
<figure class="fresh-figure" data-fresh-age>
 <div class="figure-heading"><span class="figure-number">Figure 1</span>The answer ages before the TTL begins</div>
 <div class="controls">
  <label>Delay before insertion <select data-delay><option value="0">0 seconds</option><option value="20" selected>20 seconds</option><option value="40">40 seconds</option></select></label>
  <label>Source snapshot <select data-lag><option value="0">Current at the read</option><option value="15">15 seconds behind</option></select></label>
 </div>
 <div class="scene">
  <div class="row" data-live>
   <div class="box"><strong>Source read</strong><span>t = 0 s</span><span data-snapshot>Snapshot from t = 0 s</span></div>
   <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
   <div class="box"><strong>Insert copy</strong><span data-insert>t = 20 s</span><span data-age>Already 20 s old</span></div>
   <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
   <div class="box"><strong>Entry expires</strong><span data-expire>t = 50 s</span><span data-end-age>Observation age reaches 50 s</span></div>
  </div>
  <p data-live data-scale>Bars share a scale from t = 0 s to t = 50 s.</p>
  <p><strong>Age of the source observation</strong> <span data-live data-age-label>0 → 50 seconds</span></p>
  <div class="track" aria-hidden="true"><span class="age-span" style="left:0;width:100%"></span></div>
  <p><strong>Time allowed by insertion TTL</strong> <span>30 seconds</span></p>
  <div class="track" aria-hidden="true"><span data-ttl-bar style="left:40%;width:60%"></span></div>
  <p class="callout" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">The twenty-second delay uses twenty seconds of a thirty-second age allowance. Only ten seconds remain when the copy enters the cache.</p>
 </div>
 <figcaption>Invented timings. The upper bar starts at the source snapshot; the lower bar starts at insertion. The replica option assumes its snapshot age is known exactly. A real replica needs a trustworthy bound before its lag can enter this calculation.</figcaption>
 <details><summary>The timeline as text</summary><p>With a current source and a twenty-second delay, observe at 0, insert at 20, and expire at 50. A thirty-second maximum observation age instead ends reuse at 30. If the source snapshot was already fifteen seconds behind at the read, the inserted copy is thirty-five seconds old and must be rejected under that age rule.</p></details>
</figure>
<script>
 import './age.mjs';
</script>
